    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="1427" n="1313" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1313"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> J.C.S. Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the United States Chiefs of
                        Staff</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d636-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/> C.C.S. 332</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-08-31">31 August 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Propaganda Plans</hi>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Lack of clear understanding between theater commanders and the Combined
                        Chiefs of Staff concerning the propaganda to be used in furtherance of
                        agreed operations has led to discrepancies which have had embarrassing
                        implications.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Effective coordination between the theaters and all propaganda agencies of
                        the United Nations can be assured if propaganda plans are prepared and
                        approved in advance of operations. It is therefore recommended that the
                        attached directive to all theater commanders be approved by the Combined
                        Chiefs of Staff.</item>
                </list>



                <xi:include href="d636-a1.xml" xpointer="d636-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
